			"description" : "{Arcanomechanical Amulet}\r\n\r\nArcanomechanical Amulet causes all war machines to be treated as arcanomechanical devices, and they become invulnerable. If you have not learned Enchantment, your Snipper and Destroyer gain the most basic enchantment effects. If you have already learned it, their enchantment tier is enhanced.\r\nThe effects corresponding to each Enchantment level are as follows:\r\n\tNone: Snipper can adds a Lightning Bolt after each attack, dealing 20 + 10 × hero level damage.Destroyer can shoots Fireball on attack.\r\n\tBasic: Snipper can adds a Titan Bolt after each attack, dealing 35 + 15 × hero level damage. Destroyer can shoots Inferno on attack.\r\n\tAdvanced: Snipper can adds an Air Implosion after each attack, dealing 50 + 20 × hero level damage. Destroyer can shoots Flame Storm on attack.\r\n\tExpert: Snipper can adds a Chain Lightning Ex after each attack, dealing 65 + 25 × hero level damage. Destroyer can shoots Armageddon Ex on attack.\r\n{Twinborn} - When you have learned Enchantment, Amber can cast the corresponding level of Weak Spell Mark:\r\n\tBasic: Reduces the target’s all spell resistances by 50%.\r\n\t Advanced: Reduces the target’s all spell resistances by 75%. \r\n\tExpert: Reduces the target’s all spell resistances by 100%.",
			"event" : "You find yourself playing rock-paper-scissors with a drunkard in the tavern, and luck smiles warmly upon you as you win his last three gold coins. Desperate, he pulls out an heirloom amulet—his final wager. Yet the Lady of Fortune still refuses to stand by his side. With a satisfied grin, you claim the amulet and tuck it safely into your pack."
